# Archived snapshot: `historical/previous_implementations/complete_implementation_2026-05-28/Full_Proof_Skeleton.lean`

The original text of this file is preserved verbatim in the git history:

    git show b4001a7:historical/previous_implementations/complete_implementation_2026-05-28/Full_Proof_Skeleton.lean

(sha256 `68247ff413f340e05449f88ffab1ebe4d681f171a4b17203eed86c4df8157efd`, listed in `historical/ARCHIVED_LEAN_SNAPSHOTS.md`).

That text was never compiled by the kernel-certificate build: it was outside the lake
libraries, it imported modules that do not exist in this tree, and it contained 9 uses of `sorry`/`axiom` outside comments. It proves nothing and is not part of any claim.

This file now contains only this note, so that every tracked `.lean` file is compiled with
no `sorry` and no custom axiom. The kernel-checked development is the `NS_Millennium_Proof`
library; see `README.md`.
